Package: omniacli-workspaces
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: OmniaSolutions <matteo.boscolo@omniasolutions.eu>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: omniacli (= @VERSION@), nginx, certbot
Recommends: docker.io | docker-ce, docker-compose-v2 | docker-compose-plugin | docker-compose (>= 2)
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: what OmniaCLI's workspaces need on the machine
 The customers' workspaces of OmniaCLI (README, Workspaces) publish each
 instance on its domain through nginx, with a certificate of Let's Encrypt
 made and renewed by certbot, and run the instances in Docker Compose. This
 package installs nginx and certbot, and Docker with its compose plugin when
 the machine has none (docker.io or Docker's own docker-ce satisfy it).
 Debian 12 has no compose plugin of its own (its docker-compose is 1.29): there
 install Docker's docker-ce and docker-compose-plugin.
 .
 It changes no setting: the workspaces are still allowed with
 OMNIACLI_WORKSPACES=1 in /etc/default/omniacli.
